/-!
# Canonical finite core of an actual whole-restart crossing

An actual half-critical whole contact internally selects the first canonical
sharp radius whose finite core has already crossed the same threshold.  The
selected core is recompiled exactly as primitive finite raw-source data, while
the omitted tail remains on the original whole carrier.  Before any finite
physical endpoint is generated, the whole/core difference is retained exactly
in both Euclidean mass and every infinite nonlinear output row.

The radius is generated by `Nat.find`; it is not accepted in any public theorem
mouth.  This module does not identify a finite Galerkin endpoint with the actual
whole update.
-/

namespace SaturationMonoid
namespace NavierStokes
namespace
  ThreeDimensionalVorticityCoefficientGeneratedWholeRestartCrossingFiniteCore

